## Summary

| Type | Damage | Sharp penetration | Blunt penetration | Range |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ballistic | mid | mid | mid | mid |
| laser | high(burn) | low | mid | low |
| gauss | low | low | high | high |

## Open flags (not yet resolved, review before applying to real XML)
1. Ballistic Incendiary/EMP rows are exact copies of QaP/Ni — only laser/gauss math makes them numerically distinct.
2. Chain Shotgun's new "Normal" row reuses QaP/Ni values (already identical to each other).
3. `BOR_Gun_GaussShotgun_TI` TC row changes character: was 16-pellet (dmg 15) in the original file, is now single-hit (dmg 6) since it's derived from Chain Shotgun's single-target TC row.
